{"name":"Apple Valley","hex":"#ea8386","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Apple Valley","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in San Bernardino County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Apple_Valley"}],"entries":[{"title":"Apple Valley, California","blocks":[{"text":"Apple Valley is an incorporated town in the Victor Valley of San Bernardino County, California, United States. Its population was 75,791 as of the 2020 United States census. The town is east of and adjoining to the neighboring cities of Victorville and Hesperia, 35 miles (56 km) south of Barstow, and 49 miles (79 km) north of San Bernardino through the Cajon Pass. It was incorporated on November 14, 1988, and is one of the 22 incorporated municipalities in California that use \"town\" in their names instead of \"city\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Apple_Valley_from_Bass_Hill_Trail.jpg/330px-Apple_Valley_from_Bass_Hill_Trail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Valley%2C_California","wikidata":"Q621372"},{"title":"Apple Valley, Georgia","blocks":[{"text":"Apple Valley is an unincorporated community in Jackson County, in the U.S. state of Georgia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Valley%2C_Georgia","wikidata":"Q54888451"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"},{"title":"Valley","blocks":[{"text":"A valley is an elongated low area often running between hills or mountains and typically containing a river or stream running from one end to the other. Most valleys are formed by erosion of the land surface by rivers or streams over a very long period. Some valleys are formed through erosion by glacial ice. These glaciers may remain present in valleys in high mountains or polar areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG/330px-Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley","wikidata":"Q39816"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Seal_of_Apple_Valley%2C_California.png/120px-Seal_of_Apple_Valley%2C_California.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e1/Seal_of_Apple_Valley%2C_California.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Seal_of_Apple_Valley%2C_California.png/120px-Seal_of_Apple_Valley%2C_California.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeal_of_Apple_Valley%2C_California.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Malus_domestica_a1.jpg/500px-Malus_domestica_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Malus_domestica_a1.jpg/500px-Malus_domestica_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn